  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CACI Federal posted $2.1B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 188 awards, with an average award size of $11.2M. CACI Federal obligations are down 40.2% year over year. CACI Federal received the largest share of dollars from the Department of Defense, which obligated $1.1B, followed by the General Services Administration at $728M and the Department of Homeland Security at $150M. CACI Federal work is concentrated in Computer Systems Design Services at $855M and Engineering Services at $525M, with additional activity in Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $194M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $162M. CACI Federal obligations by fiscal year show a peak at $3.5B in FY25 and a decline to $2.1B in FY26 so far. CACI Federal sells a mix of IT, engineering, research, and professional services across civilian and defense agencies, and the current-year totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has CACI Federal's federal revenue trended recently?",
        "body": "CACI Federal obligations rose from $1.3B in FY21 to $3.5B in FY25 before falling to $2.1B in FY26 to date. CACI Federal obligations are down 40.2% year over year in the current fiscal year to date. CACI Federal counted 188 awards in FY2026 to date and an average award size of $11.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and which markets matter most?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.1B, with the General Services Administration next at $728M and the Department of Homeland Security at $150M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for CACI Federal at $855M, followed by Engineering Services at $525M and Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $194M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does CACI Federal make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "CACI Federal has $2.1B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. CACI Federal recorded 188 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $11.2M, and obligations are down 40.2% year over year. Historical obligations for CACI Federal were $1.3B in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $2.3B in FY23, $2.8B in FY24, and $3.5B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from CACI Federal?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer from CACI Federal, obligating $1.1B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $728M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $150M in FY2026 to date. Other buying agencies in FY2026 to date include NASA at $111M, the Department of the Interior at $24.9M, the Department of Commerce at $1.1M, and the Department of Health and Human Services at $0."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does CACI Federal sell to the government?",
      "a": "CACI Federal sells primarily IT and engineering and professional services. The largest NAICS markets for CACI Federal in FY2026 to date are Computer Systems Design Services at $855M and Engineering Services at $525M, with additional work in Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $194M and research in the physical, engineering, and life sciences at $162M."
